-- ============================================================================
-- DR4 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Well Control, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the span walk and the shut-in reading. The mud column
-- as the primary barrier and the preventer as the secondary one. Flow out
-- before pit gain, because the first is a rate and the second is its integral.
-- Volumes and stroke counts from a section by section walk down the string and
-- up the annulus, with measured depth for volumes and true vertical depth for
-- pressures. The drill pipe as a manometer, and the three things that break
-- it: a float, a plugged bit, and the string off bottom. Kill mud as a
-- deficit converted to a density and added. And the two kill methods, which
-- differ only in when the kill mud is pumped.
--
-- THE LESSONS TEACH THESE QUANTITIES ON THE HORIZONTAL WELL AND THE CAPSTONE
-- GRADES THE SLANT ONE. That is forced rather than stylistic: the Associate
-- fields are volumes and depths, and the horizontal well's are published in
-- the goldens. Grading the well the lessons walk would have graded a number a
-- learner could read out of a table.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling against its own goldens, and the teaching lab that the
-- panels and this course share is pinned to the same values by
-- wellcontrolLab.test.js. A numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 157
-- literals carrying seven or more significant figures to an engine-derived
-- value; a tier-leakage sweep over the lessons and the banks reports zero
-- downward leaks and zero same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded
-- fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('wellcontrol', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-what-a-kick-is","title":"What a Kick Is","lesson_keys":["l01-the-primary-barrier","l02-causes-and-warning-signs","l03-shut-in-and-why-quickly","l04-what-the-answer-is-for"]},{"key":"m02-volumes-and-strokes","title":"Volumes and Strokes","lesson_keys":["l01-the-span-walk","l02-string-and-annulus","l03-pump-output-and-efficiency","l04-the-two-depths","l05-capacity-at-a-depth"]},{"key":"m03-the-shut-in-pressures","title":"The Shut-In Pressures","lesson_keys":["l01-the-drill-pipe-is-a-manometer","l02-formation-pressure-from-sidpp","l03-why-the-casing-reads-higher","l04-when-the-drill-pipe-lies","l05-reading-them-in-order"]},{"key":"m04-the-kill-mud","title":"The Kill Mud","lesson_keys":["l01-what-weight-balances-it","l02-the-trip-margin","l03-mixing-it-and-the-delay","l04-what-if-you-cannot-make-it"]},{"key":"m05-circulating-it-out","title":"Circulating It Out","lesson_keys":["l01-two-methods","l02-the-drillers-method","l03-wait-and-weight","l04-which-one-and-why","l05-the-slow-circulating-rate"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'wellcontrol' and tier = 'beginner';

